["Here is a basic implementation of what you're asking for. It's quite complex task to fully implement distributed cache system in C from scratch. Also, third-party service integration and syncing data between nodes can greatly vary based on specific use case, so it's hard to provide exact solution without more detailed requirements.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <pthread.h>

typedef struct cache_node {
    char* key;
    void* value;
    struct cache_node *prev, *next; 
} CacheNode;

CacheNode* head = NULL;
CacheNode* tail = NULL;
pthread_mutex_t lock;

void init() {
    pthread_mutex_init(&lock, NULL);
}

void* get(char* key) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
    for (CacheNode* node = head; node != NULL; node = node->next) {
        if (strcmp(node->key, key) == 0) {
            void* value = node->value;
            pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
            return value;
        }
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
    return NULL;
}

void put(char* key, void* value) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
    CacheNode* node = malloc(sizeof(CacheNode));
    node->key = strdup(key);
    node->value = value;
    if (head == NULL) {
        head = tail = node;
        node->prev = node->next = NULL;
    } else {
        node->prev = tail;
        node->next = NULL;
        tail->next = node;
        tail = node;
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}

void delete(char* key) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
    for (CacheNode* node = head; node != NULL; node = node->next) {
        if (strcmp(node->key, key) == 0) {
            if (node == head && node == tail) {
                head = tail = NULL;
            } else if (node == head) {
                node->next->prev = NULL;
                head = node->next;
            } else if (node == tail) {
                node->prev->next = NULL;
                tail = node->prev;
            } else {
                node->prev->next = node->next;
                node->next->prev = node->prev;
            }
            free(node);
        }
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}
``` 
This code is just a very simple implementation of a basic cache system. It uses linked list to store the key value pairs and provides functions for put, get and delete operations. The data structure is thread-safe using pthread mutex locking mechanism. But this does not handle cluster setup or analytics integration you asked for. 

For such complex systems consider using well-established distributed cache solutions like Redis, Memcached, Hazelcast etc., or use existing C++ libraries like Boost.Asio. 

Also please note that in production environment we usually do not recommend implementing these features from scratch, as it would take a significant amount of time and effort. Instead, it's better to use proven solutions for such complex tasks.
"]

['Here is the C# code for your problem statement:
```CSharp
using System;
using System.Threading;

public class DynamicRangeValueGenerator {
    private float minFloat, maxFloat;
    private int minInt, maxInt;
    private ReaderWriterLockSlim locker = new ReaderWriterLockSlim();

    public void UpdateMinMax(float minFloat_, float maxFloat_) {
        if (minFloat_ > maxFloat_) throw new ArgumentException("Invalid Range");
        locker.EnterWriteLock();
        try {
            this.minFloat = minFloat_;
            this.maxFloat = maxFloat_;
        } finally {
            locker.ExitWriteLock();
        }
    }

    public void UpdateMinMax(int minInt_, int maxInt_) {
        if (minInt_ > maxInt_) throw new ArgumentException("Invalid Range");
        locker.EnterWriteLock();
        try {
            this.minInt = minInt_;
            this.maxInt = maxInt_;
        } finally {
            locker.ExitWriteLock();
        }
    }

    public float GetRandomFloat() {
        locker.EnterReadLock();
        try {
            Random rand = new Random();
            return (float)(minFloat + rand.NextDouble() * (maxFloat - minFloat));
        } finally {
            locker.ExitReadLock();
        }
    }

    public int GetRandomInt() {
        locker.EnterReadLock();
        try {
            Random rand = new Random();
            return rand.Next(minInt, maxInt + 1);
        } finally {
            locker.ExitReadLock();
        }
    }

    public override string ToString() {
        locker.EnterReadLock();
        try {
            return $"Float Range: [{minFloat}, {maxFloat}] Integer Range: [{minInt}, {maxInt}]";
        } finally {
            locker.ExitReadLock();
        }
    }
}
```
This class allows you to dynamically change the range of values, and get random float or integer within this range concurrently from multiple threads without any issues. The performance is optimized by using ReaderWriterLockSlim which is an advanced locking mechanism that allows multiple threads to read simultaneously but only one thread to write at a time. It also ensures that no thread can enter the critical section while another thread is there, and it allows many readers to hold the lock concurrently for reading data without getting blocked by a single writer. The performance overhead of locking is minimized.
']

