['Here is a possible solution using `Random` for generating random numbers within given range. Please note that `volatile` keyword can guarantee read/write of value on main memory (not CPU's cache) which prevents caching issues. `Interlocked` class is used to handle concurrent updates from multiple threads safely.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading;
using System.Text;

public class MultiDimensionalValueGenerator
{
    private int[] minBoundaries, maxBoundaries;

    public MultiDimensionalValueGenerator(int[] minBoundaries, int[] maxBoundaries)
    {
        if (minBoundaries == null || maxBoundaries == null || minBoundaries.Length != maxBoundaries.Length)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid boundaries");

        this.minBoundaries = minBoundaries;
        this.maxBoundaries = maxBoundaries;
    }

    public int[] GetRandomVector(bool inclusive, Random rand)
    {
        if (rand == null) throw new ArgumentNullException("rand");

        var vector = new int[minBoundaries.Length];
        for (int i = 0; i < minBoundaries.Length; ++i)
            vector[i] = rand.Next(minBoundaries[i], maxBoundaries[i] + (inclusive ? 1 : 0));

        return vector;
    }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < minBoundaries.Length; ++i)
            sb.AppendFormat("[{0}, {1}] ", minBoundaries[i], maxBoundaries[i]);

        return sb.ToString().TrimEnd();
    }

    public void UpdateDimension(int dimension, int newMin, int newMax)
    {
        if (dimension < 0 || dimension >= minBoundaries.Length) 
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid dimension");

        Interlocked.Exchange(ref minBoundaries[dimension], newMin);
        Interlocked.Exchange(ref maxBoundaries[dimension], newMax);
    }
}
```
In this code, `UpdateDimension` function is designed to change the boundary of a dimension safely while keeping it thread-safe and efficient. The boundaries are kept in an array for each dimension which allows easy update or fetch operation with index. 

A few things to note:
1. Error handling is basic here. In reality, you might want more detailed error messages that include information about what specifically went wrong.
2. This class currently assumes all dimensions have the same type (integer). If different types are needed in the future, a more sophisticated design could be considered.
3. The `Random` instance provided to the `GetRandomVector` method should ideally come from a thread-safe source like a global singleton or similar to ensure that no two threads use the same random number generator at once.
4. This code does not provide any mechanism for handling external changes in the boundary values. If these can change dynamically, you'll need to add appropriate methods for updating them and potentially synchronization mechanisms to avoid race conditions when updating the boundaries from multiple threads simultaneously.
