This solution uses mutexes for ensuring thread safety. It validates the URL, cache and callback function concurrently avoiding race conditions while checking null pointers and empty strings for the URL. If any check fails, it returns a corresponding error code. The locking mechanism ensures that only one thread is modifying the data at a time, improving performance on multithreaded environments. 

