            String uniqueIdentifier;
            try {
                MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
                byte[] hashBytes = md.digest(filename.getBytes());
                uniqueIdentifier = ENCODER.encodeToString(hashBytes).substring(0, Math.min(generator == null ? filename.length() : generator.apply(obj, MAX_LENGTH - filename.length()).length(), MAX_LENGTH - filename.length()));
            } catch (Exception e) {
                throw new RuntimeException("Failed to generate unique identifier", e);
            }

            String extension = "";
            int extIndex = filename.lastIndexOf('.');
            if (extIndex != -1 && extIndex < filename.length() - 1) {
                extension = filename.substring(extIndex);
                filename = filename.substring(0, extIndex);
            }

            String newFilename = generator == null ? filename + uniqueIdentifier : filename + generator.apply(obj, MAX_LENGTH - filename.length() - extension.length()) + extension;
            if (newFilename.length() > MAX_LENGTH) {
                throw new RuntimeException("Modified filename exceeds maximum length of 128 characters");
            }

            return newFilename;
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException(e);
        }
    }

    private interface ModifiableInterface {}
}
```

This implementation assumes the existence of an `ModifiableInterface` that must be implemented by deserialized objects. The checksum generation is performed using SHA-256 and Base64 encoding. A custom identifier generator function can optionally be provided to customize identifier generation logic. If a custom generator is not provided, the original filename length is used as a base for the identifier.
']

