['Your task requires a deep understanding of C programming, concurrency, memory management, logging, performance optimization, and telemetry systems. Below is a simplified example of how such module can be implemented in C using POSIX thread and pthread_mutex. However, please note that creating real-life network management system library would require a much more complex solution with error checking, robust error handling, proper memory management, logging mechanism, and so on.

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>

// Structure definition
typedef struct UE_Context {
    int UE_ID;
    int MACs[10]; // Assume a max of 10 MAC entities for each UE
    float PDCP_statistics;
} UE_Context;

// Mutex for thread safety
pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

// Array of UE Contexts
UE_Context* ue_contexts;
int num_ues = 0;

void* add_mac(void *arg) {
    // Lock the mutex to prevent concurrent access
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    int UE_ID = *((int*) arg);
    ue_contexts[UE_ID].MACs[0] = 1; // Add a MAC entity (for simplicity)

    // Unlock the mutex to allow other threads to access
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}

void* update_pdcp(void *arg) {
    // Lock the mutex to prevent concurrent access
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    int UE_ID = *((int*) arg);
    ue_contexts[UE_ID].PDCP_statistics = 0.1; // Update PDCP statistics (for simplicity)

    // Unlock the mutex to allow other threads to access
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}

void* suspend_ue(void *arg) {
    // Lock the mutex to prevent concurrent access
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    int UE_ID = *((int*) arg);
    ue_contexts[UE_ID].PDCP_statistics = 0.0; // Suspend UE by setting PDCP statistics to 0

    // Unlock the mutex to allow other threads to access
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}

int main() {
    num_ues = 10; // For simplicity, assuming we have 10 UEs
    ue_contexts = (UE_Context*) calloc(num_ues, sizeof(UE_Context));

    for (int i=0;i<num_ues;i++) {
        ue_contexts[i].UE_ID = i;

        // Create thread to add MAC entity and update PDCP statistics for each UE
        pthread_t t1, t2, t3;
        pthread_create(&t1, NULL, add_mac, &i);
        pthread_create(&t2, NULL, update_pdcp, &i);
        pthread_create(&t3, NULL, suspend_ue, &i);

        // Wait for all threads to finish before continuing
        pthread_join(t1, NULL);
        pthread_join(t2, NULL);
        pthread_join(t3, NULL);
    }

    free(ue_contexts); // Free memory when finished

    return 0;
}
```
In above example, we have used POSIX thread to handle concurrent access by different threads. We also use mutex to prevent data race condition while accessing shared resource (UE Context array). This is a very basic implementation and does not include the full functionality you requested as it would take much more space and complexity. However, this should give you an idea of how to start implementing such a library in C.
']

